   "subject": "Setting Limits on a Correlation Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Is it currently possible to specify a correlation matrix with common restrictions on the support for all matrix entries (or at least the non-diagonals)? Such that the below could be specified and compile <span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">successfully:</span><div><br></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">corr_matrix</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">&lt;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">lower</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,134,179);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">,</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">upper</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,134,179);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">1</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">[D] restrictedMatrix;</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></div><div>An equivalent solution would be a general <span style=\"color:rgb(167,29,93);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">[D,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">D</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">]</span> with diagonals = 1, non-diagonals restricted between 0 and 1 and with symmetry enforced, but I&#39;ve been unable to specify such a matrix. </div><div><br></div><div>A related question is whether setting this type of restriction on a correlation matrix is even a good idea in the first place from a sampling perspective, is it liable to result in poor HMC behaviour?</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
