     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>No<br> </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\"></span>An equivalent solution would be a general <span style=\"color:rgb(167,29,93);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">[D,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">D</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">]</span> with diagonals = 1, non-diagonals restricted between 0 and 1 and with symmetry enforced, but I&#39;ve been unable to specify such a matrix. </div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>Also, you are ignoring the restriction that the correlation matrix be positive definite, which is very difficult to satisfy for correlation matrices that are larger then 3 rows and columns.<br> </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>A related question is whether setting this type of restriction on a correlation matrix is even a good idea in the first place from a sampling perspective, is it liable to result in poor HMC behaviour?</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>Generally a bad idea. If you think the correlations will tend not to be far from zero, increase the value of the shape parameter in the LKJ prior.<br><br>Also, it is usually better to make the parameter a cholesky_factor_corr[D] rather than a corr_matrix[D].<br><br><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
